---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const jobs = [
  {
    company: "W.W. Grainger",
    location: "Chicago, IL",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Software Engineer",
        period: "May 2022 - Present",
        type: "Full-time",
        bullets: [
          "Working with Customer Orders - this means 1.3M+ Kafka events per day, seven years of searchable order history, and millions of active accounts. The kind of scale where getting something wrong is immediately visible.",
          "Built the HTTP APIs that make orders searchable across channels. Re-orders from that history account for roughly 6% of Grainger's order revenue - a number that's easy to forget is backed by code someone has to maintain.",
          "Kafka event pipeline provides real-time order status to downstream systems: email notifications, mobile notifications, tracking, order displays across the platform. Designing for at-least-once delivery with idempotent consumers took a few iterations to get right.",
          "Spring Boot/Kotlin microservices feed Databricks and Snowflake pipelines for both operational and analytical use - two different read patterns with different freshness requirements.",
          "Led the Order Detail Experience project from design through production. Also owned HCP Vault Migration and a DBaaS migration, both with near-zero production impact.",
          "Diagnosed and fixed a high-severity auth misconfiguration in production - shipped a targeted fix, wrote the postmortem, and turned it into a team learning session rather than a blame exercise.",
          "Run architecture and engineering practice sessions for the team. Started as informal conversations, turned into something the team now expects.",
        ],
        tags: ["Java", "Kotlin", "Spring Boot", "Python", "Kafka", "Databricks", "Snowflake", "SQL", "NoSQL", "AWS", "Docker", "DataDog"],
      },
      {
        title: "Software Engineer",
        period: "Feb 2021 - May 2022",
        type: "via IT Syntax, Inc.",
        bullets: [
          "Same Customer Order codebase - backend services in Java and Kotlin, Kafka-driven pipelines, Spring Boot microservices handling the order lifecycle.",
          "Brought into architecture reviews and code standards conversations early on; applied TDD with JUnit and Mockito across the team.",
        ],
        tags: ["Java", "Kotlin", "Kafka", "Spring Boot", "JUnit"],
      },
      {
        title: "Software Engineer",
        period: "Nov 2019 - Jan 2021",
        type: "via Code Gravity, LLC",
        bullets: [
          "B2B and B2C e-commerce on SAP Hybris - cart and checkout, account management, order approvals, replenishment - serving millions of transactions across Grainger's catalog of millions of SKUs.",
          "Built Impex scripts, cron jobs, and feature toggles for real-time product, pricing, and promotion management. Some of these ran every few minutes in production.",
          "Spring Boot microservices with REST APIs (Java 11); Cassandra for session and cart persistence.",
          "Supported Hypercare post-Go-Live, ran root cause analysis on production incidents, managed CI/CD via Maven and Git.",
        ],
        tags: ["Java", "SAP Hybris", "Spring Boot", "Cassandra", "Maven", "CI/CD"],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    company: "GuideWell Florida Blue",
    location: "Jacksonville, FL",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Software Engineer",
        period: "Feb 2019 - Nov 2019",
        type: "via Code Gravity, LLC",
        bullets: [
          "Full-stack application for one of the largest US healthcare insurers - millions of members, real compliance requirements, and a team spread across multiple time zones.",
          "Containerized microservices on Kubernetes and OpenShift; handled auto-scaling, service discovery, and on-call support through production launch.",
          "Spring Data with PostgreSQL and MongoDB on the backend; AngularJS frontend with client-side validations and REST/SOAP integrations.",
          "First time I had to care deeply about deployment infrastructure, not just the code. Kubernetes makes you think differently about failure modes.",
        ],
        tags: ["Spring Boot", "AngularJS", "PostgreSQL", "MongoDB", "Kubernetes", "OpenShift", "Kafka"],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    company: "Aflac",
    location: "Columbus, GA",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Application Developer",
        period: "Aug 2017 - Jan 2019",
        type: "via Capricorn Systems, Inc.",
        bullets: [
          "Frontend-heavy role - HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, Bootstrap, jQuery. Spent a lot of time on cross-browser issues and mobile responsiveness.",
          "Content management via Crownpeak CMS and SharePoint; CTA split-screen designs for mobile users. Got good at making things work on devices I couldn't test on.",
          "Documented system architecture with UML; worked in weekly Agile sprints. My first experience of what 'working software over comprehensive documentation' actually means in practice.",
        ],
        tags: ["HTML5", "CSS3", "JavaScript", "Bootstrap", "jQuery", "Crownpeak CMS", "Agile"],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    company: "Infosys",
    location: "India",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Software Engineer Intern",
        period: "Jan 2015 - May 2015",
        type: "",
        bullets: [
          "Training in software testing, data warehouse concepts, and T-SQL.",
          "Led a three-person team to deliver a \"Text Based Pattern Lock for Android\" - my first time owning something from idea to working demo.",
        ],
        tags: ["Java", "T-SQL", "Android", "JUnit"],
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title="Experience · Veera Annapureddy" current="experience">

  <section class="exp-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h4>Career</h4>
      <h2>Where I've worked</h2>
      <hr class="divider" />
      <p class="exp-hero__sub">Eight years across e-commerce, healthcare, and insurance. Most of it at scale, all of it in teams.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="exp-list">
    <div class="container container--wide">
      {jobs.map((job) => (
        <div class="company">
          <div class="company__header">
            <div>
              <h3 class="company__name">{job.company}</h3>
              <span class="company__loc">{job.location}</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          {job.roles.map((role, i) => (
            <div class={`role ${i > 0 ? 'role--sub' : ''}`}>
              <div class="role__meta">
                <span class="role__title">{role.title}</span>
                <span class="role__period">{role.period}</span>
                {role.type && <span class="role__type">{role.type}</span>}
              </div>

              <ul class="role__bullets">
                {role.bullets.map(b => <li>{b}</li>)}
              </ul>

              <div class="role__tags">
                {role.tags.map(t => <span class="tag">{t}</span>)}
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="edu">
    <div class="container">
      <h4>Education</h4>
      <h2>Academic background</h2>
      <hr class="divider" />
      <div class="edu__grid">
        <div class="edu__item">
          <span class="edu__degree">M.S. Computer Science</span>
          <span class="edu__school">Columbus State University</span>
          <span class="edu__detail">Columbus, GA · 2017</span>
        </div>
        <div class="edu__item">
          <span class="edu__degree">B.Tech Computer Science &amp; Engineering</span>
          <span class="edu__school">KL University</span>
          <span class="edu__detail">Andhra Pradesh, India · 2015</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
.exp-hero {
  padding: 5rem 0 3rem;
}

.exp-hero__sub {
  color: var(--ink-muted);
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  max-width: 480px;
  margin: 0;
}

.exp-list {
  padding-top: 1rem;
}

.company {
  margin-bottom: 4rem;
  padding-bottom: 4rem;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}

.company:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
  margin-bottom: 0;
  padding-bottom: 0;
}

.company__header {
  margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
}

.company__name {
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
}

.company__loc {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: var(--ink-faint);
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
}

.role {
  margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
}

.role--sub {
  padding-top: 2rem;
  border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
}

.role__meta {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: baseline;
  gap: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.role__title {
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  color: var(--ink);
}

.role__period {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: var(--ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
}

.role__type {
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  color: var(--ink-faint);
  font-style: italic;
}

.role__bullets {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.65rem;
}

.role__bullets li {
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  color: var(--ink-muted);
  padding-left: 1.1rem;
  position: relative;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.role__bullets li::before {
  content: "-";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  color: var(--border-dark);
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  top: 0.12em;
}

.role__tags {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.4rem;
}

/* ── Education ─────────────────────────────────── */
.edu__grid {
  display: flex;
  gap: 3rem;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.edu__item {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.25rem;
}

.edu__degree {
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  color: var(--ink);
}

.edu__school {
  font-size: 0.875rem;
  color: var(--ink-muted);
}

.edu__detail {
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  color: var(--ink-faint);
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
}
</style>
